# Several suites compare committed files byte-for-byte against generator
# output that always uses LF: the duet-cli integration tests against
# examples/generated/*, the codegen goldens under packages/*/test/generated/,
# and the two corpus files. GitHub's Windows runners check repositories out
# with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text file to CRLF and fails
# all of those comparisons at once (found by the first run of the `windows`
# CI job). Force LF in every working tree instead; byte-identical means one
# spelling of a line ending, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never candidates for text auto-detection or normalization.
*.png binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
